{{also|Shown}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|schauen}}, {{m|enm|schewen|pos=past participle}}, alternative form of {{m|enm|schawid}}, {{m|enm|schewed}}, past participle of {{der|en|enm|schewen|t=to show}}. Morphologically equivalent to {{suf|en|show|n<id:past participle>}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃəʊn/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃoʊn/|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-shown.ogg|a=US}}
** {{rhymes|en|əʊn|s=1}}
** {{homophones|en|shone}} {{q|one pronunciation}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{past participle of|en|show|nocat=1}}
#: {{ux|en|I had '''shown''' him the report already.}}
#: {{ux|en|The report had already been '''shown''' to him.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Garner's Modern American Usage'' favors {{m|en|shown}} over {{m|en|showed}} as past participle and claims it is mandatory for passives. In other forms of English {{m|en|shown}} is the only correct past participle.

